For complaints that must be reported to FDA under part 803 of this chapter, complaints that a manufacturer determines must be investigated, and complaints that the manufacturer investigated regardless of those requirements, the manufacturer must record the following information:
(1) The name of the device;
(2) The date the complaint was received;
(3) Any unique device identifier (UDI) or universal product code (UPC), and any other device identification(s);
(4) The name, address, and phone number of the complainant;
(5) The nature and details of the complaint;
(6) Any correction or corrective action taken; and
(7) Any reply to the complainant.

